"The postoperative pathology reveals a Gleason 3+5 (ISUP grade group 4) diagnosis with pathological stage pT3a. Favorable findings include negative surgical margins, no invasion of the seminal vesicles, and absence of lymphovascular invasion. The absence of documented nodal sampling means that the pNx status does not establish node-negative disease, which widens the uncertainty regarding regional disease control. The biopsy findings identified Gleason 3+5 in the transition zone, with the histological growth pattern described as Acinar. Countervailing factors are limited by the lack of nodal status documentation. Postoperative PSA is not recorded, meaning biochemical recurrence cannot be assessed. Information regarding postoperative PSA and its trajectory is crucial for revising the prognosis. The fixed estimated horizon is 40.44 months. This represents expected follow-up without an event, not a known recurrence date. The sensitivity range is 26.29–54.59 months; its coverage has not been validated."
